# Applyra digest — environment variables for a LOCAL run. Copy this file to `.env` (git-ignored, never commit it).
# In GitHub Actions the values come from repository secrets/variables (README.md), never from a file.
# The digest reads only the process environment; load the file explicitly, e.g. from apps/digest:
#   node --env-file=../../.env src/main.ts

# Telegram bot token from @BotFather. Secret: never log, print or commit it.
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
# Chat id the digest goes to (your private chat with the bot, or a channel id like -100…).
# TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=

# Comma-separated source names: dou, djinni, email (`fake` works only with --dry-run).
# DIGEST_SOURCES=dou,djinni

# Source `email`: a dedicated mailbox subscribed to Work.ua / robota.ua / LinkedIn job alerts (read-only).
# Gmail: enable 2FA, create an App Password. Secret: never log, print or commit it.
# IMAP_USER=
# IMAP_PASSWORD=
# IMAP_HOST=imap.gmail.com
# IMAP_PORT=993
# authserv-id of the server whose Authentication-Results (DKIM verdict) is trusted.
# IMAP_AUTHSERV_ID=mx.google.com
# Profile file (default: profile.json, relative to apps/digest).
# DIGEST_PROFILE_PATH=
# Sent-vacancy state file (default: .state/sent.json, relative to apps/digest).
# DIGEST_STATE_PATH=

# Optional, for a future LLM scoring step (not used yet).
# LLM_API_KEY=
